{"campaign_id": "a5d7f35a-e420-46df-ae49-fbcd4467a9b6", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T19:30:27Z", "error": null, "id": "M1", "inquiry_id": null, "kind": "measurement", "request": {"description": "Characterize the compiled two-joint arm and its deterministic saturated-torque response from the singular zero reset before selecting policy development versus further physical/control characterization.", "measurements": [{"args": ["campaigns\\evaluations\\a5d7f35a-e420-46df-ae49-fbcd4467a9b6\\compiled_dynamics_probe.json"], "artifact": "campaigns\\evaluations\\a5d7f35a-e420-46df-ae49-fbcd4467a9b6\\compiled_dynamics_probe.json", "instrument": "python_module", "label": "compiled_dynamics_probe", "module": "robot_learning.lab.compiled_dynamics_probe"}], "rationale": "The unresolved initial distinction is whether the ideal reachable workspace is also dynamically usable under the compiled MuJoCo model and 50 Hz direct torque interface, or whether omitted compiled inertia/contact/default behavior makes approach and braking physically limiting. This measurement is candidate-independent and directly records the compiled quantities, inertia at reset, contact filtering, 0.2-second constant saturated-control responses, and deterministic bang-bang reversal envelopes. If responses are finite, reproducible, and contact-free with effective actuator authority consistent with the model, the next direction should be fresh policy development with reach-and-hold diagnostics. If authority is weak, the envelope fails to brake, inertia/coupling is unexpectedly large, or contacts appear, the next direction should characterize or redesign control around that physical constraint rather than treating policy failure as a learning failure. The probe does not measure episode success or certify the human goal."}, "result": {"measurements": [{"args": ["campaigns\\evaluations\\a5d7f35a-e420-46df-ae49-fbcd4467a9b6\\compiled_dynamics_probe.json"], "instrument": "python_module", "label": "compiled_dynamics_pro